<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36588" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαίφν-ης</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>on a sudden,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				17.738
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				21.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				9.52
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				1077
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1610
			</span></i>, etc.: c. part., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχὴν
				θεωρεῖν ἐ. ἀποθανόντος ἑκάστου</span>
			<i>the moment that</i> he is dead, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				523e
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκούσαντι ἐ.</span>
			<i>at first</i> hearing, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Cra.</u>
				396b
			</span></i>: c. Art., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τό γ᾽ ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.153
				</span></i>
			; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἐ.</span>
			<i>the instantaneous,</i> that which is between motion and rest,
			and not in the time-series, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prm.</u>
				156d
			</span></i>; but, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἐν ἀναισθήτῳ χρόνῳ
					διὰ μικρότητα ἐκστάν</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				222b15
			</span></i>.</div>
